.TH IX 1
.SH NAME
ix \- indexed, ranked full-text search
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ix build
.I index.ix file...
.br
.B ix search
.I index.ix word...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Ix
is a work-alike of the information-retrieval chapter of Nelson's
.IR "Computer Lib/Dream Machines" :
an inverted index (word \(->\ which documents contain it, and how
often) built once, then a multi-word query ranked by classic TF-IDF
\(em a word's contribution to a document's score is how often it
appears there, relative to the document's own length, times how rare
that word is across the whole indexed set \(em rather than the plain
line-matching of
.IR grep (1).
.PP
.B ix build
reads every
.I file
given, tokenizes it, and writes a plain-text on-disk index to
.IR index.ix .
.B ix search
tokenizes
.I word...
the same way and prints every indexed document that contains any
query word, ranked highest score first.
.PP
Both the on-disk index and the query/rank pass are plain lists with
linear search: fine at demo scale, not written to scale further.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/ix.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR grep (1)
